## 7h — Weekly memory consolidation (Fridays only)

**Skip this step entirely if today is not Friday.**

Once per week, scan all person and project node files and collapse noise that has accumulated in the signal logs. This keeps memory files readable and context-bounded as they grow.

**Which files to scan:**
- All `memory/people/*.md`
- All `memory/projects/*.md`

**Three consolidation rules — apply all three to each file:**

**Rule 1 — No-signal collapse**
If 3 or more consecutive `[no-signal]` entries appear with adjacent dates, replace the entire run with a single line:
```
- [no-signal] Dark {N} weeks — no activity {first_date} through {last_date}
```
This is idempotent — a pre-collapsed entry won't re-collapse.

**Rule 2 — Duplicate signal merge**
If the same core fact appears in 3+ entries within any 7-day window (judge by semantic similarity — same person, same project, same sentiment, same outcome), keep the first entry and append ` (unchanged through {last_date})` to it. Delete the duplicate entries.
Example: three consecutive `[win] Person completed task X` entries → keep first, append `(unchanged through {date})`, delete the others.

**Rule 3 — Resolved commitment pruning**
In the `## Open commitments` section of person nodes, any `[x]` completed item whose resolution date is 30+ days ago can be deleted entirely. The signal log is the historical record; stale completed items are noise in the working context.

**Hard safety rules — never violate:**
- Never touch entries from the last 14 days
- Never consolidate `[fire]` or `[concern]` entries (each occurrence matters)
- Never remove an entry that contains a direct quote (text in quotation marks)
- Never consolidate if it would remove the only occurrence of a fact
- If a file had no consolidatable content, leave it untouched — do not rewrite it

**After consolidating**, append a summary to the run log entry (Step 7d):
```
**Friday consolidation:** Consolidated N entries across M files.
```
If nothing was consolidated (all files clean), write: `**Friday consolidation:** Nothing to consolidate — files clean.`

