## 7e — Git backup (two repos: private memory + public renderer)

### Part 1 — Local memory snapshot (PRIVATE — no remote, never push)

After writing all memory files (Steps 7a–7h), snapshot them in a local git repo. This gives you rollback (`git checkout HEAD~1 -- memory/people/{slug}.md`) without publishing personal data anywhere.

```bash
MEM_DIR="$HOME/.claude/projects/-Users-$(whoami)/memory"
git -C "$MEM_DIR" init -q 2>/dev/null || true
git -C "$MEM_DIR" add people/ projects/ history/ last_brief.md 2>/dev/null || true
git -C "$MEM_DIR" commit -q -m "Alfred brief {YYYY-MM-DD}" 2>/dev/null || true
```

`git init` is idempotent — safe to run every time. All three lines use `|| true` so a git failure never blocks the brief. No remote is ever configured here.

### Part 2 — Renderer sync (PUBLIC repo)

After the memory snapshot, sync only the renderer files back to the public repo. Never commit memory files or installed SKILL.md files — they contain personal data.

```bash
cp "{{BRIEFS_DIR}}/alfred-build.py" "{{REPO_DIR}}/renderer/"
cp "{{BRIEFS_DIR}}/alfred-template.html" "{{REPO_DIR}}/renderer/"
cd "{{REPO_DIR}}" && git add renderer/ && git commit -m "Alfred brief {YYYY-MM-DD}" 2>/dev/null || true
```

The `|| true` means if push fails (no network), the brief still completes — never block on git.

# Step 8 — Fire macOS notification

After the HTML is open and state is saved, fire a notification summarizing the brief. This is the push signal that tells you the brief is ready — the HTML is the reading experience.

**Compose the notification body** as: `{fire_count} fire(s) · {days_remaining} days to rollout · {top_fire_one_liner}`

**Fire via Bash** (runs in background so it doesn't block):
```
osascript << 'EOF' &
set result to display alert "Alfred — Morning Brief is ready" message "{body}" buttons {"Dismiss", "Open Brief"} default button "Open Brief"
if button returned of result is "Open Brief" then
    do shell script "open '{{BRIEFS_DIR}}/alfred-brief-{YYYY-MM-DD}.html'"
end if
EOF
```

Replace `{body}` with the actual composed string and `{YYYY-MM-DD}` with today's date. If osascript fails for any reason, log and continue — the HTML is already open.


# Rules (recap)
- No moralizing. Practical, dense.
- No greetings/filler.
- Preserve Granola citation links.
- Honor "not a fire" calibrations.
- Email: DRAFT-ONLY. Create Gmail drafts for priority unresponded emails. NEVER send.
- Slack: DRAFT-ONLY for replies. Do NOT send a Slack DM of the brief. The HTML is the brief.
- Calendar: max 4 individuals, no distros, no C-suite.
- No audio generation.
